{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.not_jonesMarkovCoefficient_sum_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.not_jonesMarkovCoefficient_sum_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L135-L146","doc":"**`JonesMarkovCoefficient_sum_eq_one` is FALSE.**\n\nAt `n = 1`, `q = 1` every summand is `0`, so the sum is `0 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.wenzlClosedForm_one_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.wenzlClosedForm_one_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L125-L133","doc":"**Every Wenzl coefficient of every partition of `n ≥ 1` vanishes at `q = 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.outer_foldl_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.outer_foldl_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L117-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.partsList_length_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.partsList_length_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L105-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.rowLen_zero_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.rowLen_zero_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L83-L103","doc":"For `n ≠ 0` the first row is nonempty: the parts sum to `n` and are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.inner_fold_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.inner_fold_zero","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L74-L81","doc":"A nonempty row folds to `0` at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.foldl_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.foldl_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L66-L72","doc":"Once a row accumulator is `0` it stays `0`, over any list of columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.qInteger_one_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.qInteger_one_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/JonesMarkovSumCounterexample.lean#L58-L64","doc":"At `q = 1` the q-integer's numerator and denominator both vanish, so Lean's\n`0/0 = 0` makes it zero for **every** `k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}